# Design System Rules

## Typography usage
- Always use the `Typography` component from `components/ui/typography.tsx` for headings, subtitles, body, and captions.
- Use the `as` prop to choose semantic tags (e.g., `h1`, `h2`, `p`, `span`) while keeping the correct typography styles.
- Avoid ad-hoc text size/weight classes on new UI unless explicitly required for a one-off.

## Standard mappings
- Main page header: `Typography` with `variant="title"` `size="l"` `weight="book"` and `as="h1"`.
- Section header: `Typography` with `variant="title"` `size="m"` `weight="book"` and `as="h2"`.
- Subsection header: `Typography` with `variant="title"` `size="s"` `weight="book"` and `as="h3"`.
- Subtitle: `Typography` with `variant="subtitle"` `size="m"` `weight="medium"` and `as="p"`.
- Body text: `Typography` with `variant="body"` and size/weight based on context.
- Caption: `Typography` with `variant="caption"` `size="s"` `weight="book"` and `as="span"`.

## If `Typography` cannot be used
Use these class combinations exactly:
- Title L: `text-[28px] leading-[40px] font-normal`
- Title M: `text-[22px] leading-[32px] font-normal`
- Title S: `text-[18px] leading-[24px] font-normal`
- Subtitle: `text-[16px] leading-[24px] font-medium`
- Body L heavy: `text-[16px] leading-[24px] font-black`
- Body L medium: `text-[16px] leading-[24px] font-medium`
- Body M heavy: `text-[14px] leading-[20px] font-black`
- Body M medium: `text-[14px] leading-[20px] font-medium`
- Body S heavy: `text-[12px] leading-[16px] font-black`
- Body S medium: `text-[12px] leading-[16px] font-medium`
- Caption: `text-[12px] leading-[16px] font-normal`
